---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSupabaseClient } from '../lib/supabase';

const supabase = getSupabaseClient();
const { data: settings } = await supabase.from('site_settings').select('contact_email').single();
const contactEmail = settings?.contact_email ?? null;

const LAST_UPDATED = '23 September 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — JTP Skulptur" description="How JTP Skulptur collects, uses, and protects your personal information.">
  <header class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-full) px-4 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="caption">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-content) px-4 py-10 sm:px-8 sm:py-14">
    <p class="caption">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-6 border-l-2 border-(--color-clay) pl-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-soft)">
      <p>
        This policy describes, in plain language, what JTP Skulptur's website actually does with personal
        information today. It has been drafted directly from the site's implementation — it is <strong>not</strong>
        {' '}a legally reviewed document. Passages marked <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> need
        input from the site owner, and ideally a qualified advisor, before this page should be relied on as a final
        policy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 leading-relaxed">
      JTP Skulptur ("we", "us") is a studio and online gallery for the sculpture of Jens Wollinger. This policy
      explains what information we collect through this website, why, and how it's handled.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Who we are</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> Registered business name, legal entity, business
      registration number, and registered address, if applicable.
      {contactEmail && (
        <>
          {' '}You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.
        </>
      )}
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Information we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">We collect the following information, only where you provide it directly:</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Contact form</strong> — your name, email address, subject, and message, when you write to us.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Newsletter</strong> — your email address, when you subscribe. We use a confirmation email (double
        opt-in) before adding you to the list, and every send includes an unsubscribe link.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Orders</strong> — your email address at checkout, and, once payment succeeds, the name and shipping
        address you give to our payment processor, Stripe. We never see or store your full card details — see
        "Payment processing" below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shopping cart</strong> — the items in your cart are kept only in your own browser (local storage) and
        are not sent to our servers until you check out.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Studio and partner accounts</strong> — staff and studio-partner ("vendor") logins are authenticated by
        email and password. This applies only to internal accounts, not to visitors or customers.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      We do not use advertising or marketing tracking. With your consent only, we use Google Analytics 4 to
      understand, in aggregate, how the website is used (pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser).
      See our
      {' '}<a href="/cookies" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">Cookies Policy</a> for exactly what is set
      and how to change your choice.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">How we use this information</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>To respond to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
      <li>To process, confirm, and fulfil orders, and to email you order confirmations.</li>
      <li>To send newsletter updates you've explicitly opted into, and to honour unsubscribe requests.</li>
      <li>To notify the relevant studio partner when an order includes a piece they need to ship.</li>
      <li>
        To understand, in aggregate, how the website is used — only if you accept analytics cookies. The legal basis
        is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time via “Cookie settings” in the footer.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Payment processing</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      All payments are handled by <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">Stripe</a>,
      on Stripe's own secure, hosted checkout page. We never receive or store your card number, expiry date, or CVC.
      Stripe passes us your order total, email, and — once payment succeeds — the shipping name and address you
      entered, so we can fulfil your order.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Who we share information with</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong>Studio partners ("vendors")</strong> — if your order includes a piece from an independent maker
        featured on the site, that partner can see the order's shipping name, address, and item details, solely to
        ship your item. They do not see your email address or any payment information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Service providers</strong> — we use Supabase (database and file storage), Stripe (payments), Resend
        (transactional email delivery), and Cloudflare (website hosting) to run this site, and — only if you accept
        analytics cookies — Google (Google Analytics 4). Each processes data on our behalf under their own security
        and privacy terms.
        <strong class="text-(--color-clay)"> [Confirm]</strong> hosting/storage region and data-processing agreements
        for each provider.
      </li>
      <li>We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for advertising purposes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">How long we keep information</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> Specific retention periods have not yet been defined.
      Order, contact, and newsletter records are currently kept indefinitely unless you ask us to delete them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> Applicable jurisdiction(s) — e.g. whether GDPR (EU/EEA
      customers) or other regional privacy law applies. Subject to that, you typically have the right to access,
      correct, delete, or export the personal information we hold about you, and to object to or restrict certain
      uses of it.
      {contactEmail ? (
        <> To exercise any of these, email us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.</>
      ) : (
        ' To exercise any of these, please contact us.'
      )}
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This website uses strictly necessary cookies and local storage and, only if you accept, Google Analytics
      cookies. We use no advertising or marketing cookies. You can change your choice at any time via “Cookie
      settings” in the footer. Full detail is in our
      <a href="/cookies" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">Cookies Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Children</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This website is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)"> [Confirm]</strong> any specific age threshold you'd like stated here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      If this policy changes, we'll update the "last updated" date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      {contactEmail ? (
        <>Questions about this policy or your information can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.</>
      ) : (
        <>Questions about this policy or your information can be sent via our <a href="/contact" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">contact page</a>.</>
      )}
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
